{"name":"Milk Moustache","hex":"#faf3e6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"milk moustache","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["White residue on one’s upper lip after taking a deep sip of milk, a milkshake, foamy coffee, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milk_moustache"}],"entries":[{"title":"Got Milk?","blocks":[{"text":"Got Milk? is an American advertising campaign encouraging the consumption of milk and dairy products. Created by the advertising agency Goodby Silverstein & Partners for the California Milk Processor Board in 1993, it was later licensed for use by milk processors and dairy farmers. It was launched in 1993 by the \"Aaron Burr\" television commercial, directed by Michael Bay. The national campaign, run by MilkPEP began to add the \"got milk?\" logo to its \"Milk Mustache\" ads in 1995."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Got_milk.svg/330px-Got_milk.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Got_Milk%3F","wikidata":"Q513278"},{"title":"Milk","blocks":[{"text":"Milk is usually a white liquid food produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk","wikidata":"Q8495"},{"title":"Moustache","blocks":[{"text":"A moustache or mustache is a growth of facial hair grown above the upper lip and under the nose of people, mostly men."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Gaishi_Nagaoka.jpg/330px-Gaishi_Nagaoka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moustache","wikidata":"Q15179"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Got_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Got_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Got_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Got_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Got_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Got_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Got Milk?\" advertising on a barn in Marathon County, Wisconsin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGot_Milk_%5E_Barn_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Melkkarussell.jpg/500px-Melkkarussell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Melkkarussell.jpg/1280px-Melkkarussell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Melkkarussell.jpg/500px-Melkkarussell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cows in a rotary milking parlor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMelkkarussell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Woman_breastfeeding_an_infant.jpg/500px-Woman_breastfeeding_an_infant.jpg?utm_sour